Let me find.

00:22:32.150 --> 00:22:33.010
Okay. Sorry.

00:22:33.010 --> 00:22:35.240
I think I was messing
around with this a lot

00:22:35.240 --> 00:22:37.440
and then I accidentally
took out that video.

00:22:38.400 --> 00:22:40.260
I had a video I really
wanted to show you guys.

00:22:40.260 --> 00:22:41.810
Let me pull it up really quick.

00:22:59.830 --> 00:23:03.110
Okay. Found it, sorry again.

00:23:03.110 --> 00:23:04.210
- [Jeanne] No worries.

00:23:09.880 --> 00:23:12.370
- Yeah, so I want to
show you guys this video

00:23:12.370 --> 00:23:15.390
because you can use
fluorescence to kind of track

00:23:15.390 --> 00:23:17.530
living cells within a living animal.

00:23:17.530 --> 00:23:20.860
And so what this video
is, is again in the liver,

00:23:20.860 --> 00:23:23.610
they're looking at cells
kind of moving around

00:23:23.610 --> 00:23:24.973
within the mouse liver.

00:23:26.350 --> 00:23:30.670
And so in green are immune
cells of the mouse liver.

00:23:30.670 --> 00:23:34.410
And what, this is somebody that
