00:23:51.810 --> 00:23:55.950
And so there's a lot of things
you can do with microscopy,

00:23:55.950 --> 00:23:57.410
with fluorescence microscopy.

00:23:57.410 --> 00:24:00.310
And there's so much information
you can get from using it.

00:24:04.380 --> 00:24:09.380
So then [indistinct]
intro to fluorescence,

00:24:10.310 --> 00:24:14.737
I just have the last poll
question to kind of gauge you,

00:24:17.538 --> 00:24:18.980
to ask you guys and have you guys think

00:24:18.980 --> 00:24:21.410
about florescence microscopy is I told you

00:24:21.410 --> 00:24:23.460
you can start looking at a
whole bunch of different things

00:24:23.460 --> 00:24:24.940
using fluorescence but what do you think

00:24:24.940 --> 00:24:25.950
is kind of the limit?

00:24:25.950 --> 00:24:27.720
Like how many different
things can you look

00:24:27.720 --> 00:24:29.863
at at once with a fluorescence microscope?

00:24:52.260 --> 00:24:53.223
Okay, cool.

00:24:54.320 --> 00:24:58.710
